                <pb facs="0637" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10649: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-07T15:00:00+08:00">December 7, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 7—10:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1101. Following from American Consul General at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 5, noon. At a point between Ichang and Itu all shipping is
                            being heavily fired upon by troops ashore. British ship <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Wanhsien</hi>, escorted by British naval vessel,
                            was heavily fired on yesterday near Itu, and latter returned the fire
                            with effectiveness. American ships will be escorted through danger zone
                            by U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Guam</hi>, now at Ichang.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
